---
wide: true
layout: layouts/base.njk
lang: en
title: "Mushroom encyclopedia"
description: "Mushrooms without myths: a catalog of edible, poisonous and medicinal species, reviews of human clinical research and supplement safety — linked to primary sources."
og_type: "website"
permalink: "/en/"
---

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  "name": "Mushroom World",
  "url": {{ (site.url + "/en/") | dump | safe }},
  "description": {{ description | dump | safe }},
  "inLanguage": "en",
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Mushroom World",
    "url": {{ site.url | dump | safe }}
  }
}
</script>

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero__aurora" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="hero__blob hero__blob--a"></span>
    <span class="hero__blob hero__blob--b"></span>
    <span class="hero__blob hero__blob--c"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="hero__gills" aria-hidden="true">
    <svg viewBox="-300 -300 600 600" width="600" height="600">
      <g stroke="var(--color-leaf)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.5">
        {% for i in range(0, 36) %}
          {% set angle = (loop.index0 / 36) * 360 %}
          <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="280" y2="0" transform="rotate({{ angle }})"/>
        {% endfor %}
      </g>
      <g fill="var(--color-leaf)" opacity="0.25">
        <circle cx="180" cy="-110" r="2"/>
        <circle cx="-220" cy="60" r="2"/>
        <circle cx="120" cy="220" r="1.5"/>
        <circle cx="-160" cy="-180" r="1.5"/>
        <circle cx="240" cy="160" r="1.5"/>
        <circle cx="-80" cy="240" r="1.5"/>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <p class="hero__eyebrow">Mushrooms and evidence-based science</p>
  <h1 class="hero__title">Mushroom World</h1>
  <p class="hero__lead">
    What is actually known about mushrooms: which species are edible and
    which are dangerous, what human clinical trials have shown, and what
    to know before buying supplements.
  </p>
  <p class="hero__note">
    Every entry is built on peer-reviewed work and links to the primary
    source. No miracle promises — only what the data supports.
  </p>
  <div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ '/en/griby/' | url }}">Mushroom catalog</a>
    <a class="btn" href="{{ '/en/stati/' | url }}">Articles and reviews</a>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="stats" aria-label="Site in numbers">
  <a class="stat" href="{{ '/en/griby/' | url }}"><span class="stat__num" data-counter="{{ collections.gribyEn.length }}">{{ collections.gribyEn.length }}</span><span class="stat__label">species in the catalog</span></a>
  <a class="stat" href="{{ '/en/issledovaniya/' | url }}"><span class="stat__num" data-counter="{{ collections.issledovaniyaEn.length }}">{{ collections.issledovaniyaEn.length }}</span><span class="stat__label">research entries</span></a>
  <a class="stat" href="{{ '/en/stati/' | url }}"><span class="stat__num" data-counter="{{ collections.statiEn.length }}">{{ collections.statiEn.length }}</span><span class="stat__label">articles and reviews</span></a>
  <a class="stat" href="{{ '/en/temy/' | url }}"><span class="stat__num" data-counter="{{ collections.temyEn.length }}">{{ collections.temyEn.length }}</span><span class="stat__label">topic sections</span></a>
</div>

<section aria-labelledby="species" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
  <h2 id="species" style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">From the catalog</h2>
  <div class="species-strip">
    {% set shown = 0 %}
    {% for g in collections.gribyEn %}
      {% if g.data.image and shown < 14 %}
        {% set shown = shown + 1 %}
        <a class="species-chip" href="{{ g.url | url }}">
          <img src="{{ g.data.image | url }}" alt="{{ g.data.title }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <span class="species-chip__body">
            <span class="species-chip__name">{{ g.data.title }}</span>
            <span class="species-chip__latin">{{ g.data.latin_name }}</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top: var(--space-2);"><a href="{{ '/en/griby/' | url }}">Full catalog →</a></p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="topics" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
  <h2 id="topics" style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">Topics</h2>
  <div class="topic-grid">
    {% for t in collections.temyEn %}
      <a class="topic-tile" href="{{ t.url | url }}">
        <h3 class="topic-tile__title">{{ t.data.title }}</h3>
        <p class="topic-tile__lead">{{ t.data.description or t.data.lead or "" }}</p>
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="latest" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
  <h2 id="latest" style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">Latest materials</h2>

  {% if collections.statiEn.length == 0 %}
    <p class="empty">No published materials yet.</p>
  {% else %}
    <div class="card-grid">
      {% for item in collections.statiEn | reverse %}
        {% if loop.index <= 6 %}
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="card__title">
              <a href="{{ item.url | url }}" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">{{ item.data.title }}</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="card__summary">{{ (item.data.summary or item.data.description or "") | excerpt(160) }}</p>
            <div class="card__meta">
              <time datetime="{{ item.date | isoDate }}">{{ item.date | isoDate }}</time>
              {% if item.data.tags %}
                <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                <span>{{ item.data.tags[0] }}</span>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </article>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="about-short" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
  <h2 id="about-short" style="font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">About the project</h2>
  <p style="max-width: 640px; color: var(--color-text-muted);">
    Mushroom World is an independent reference about fungi. We collect
    and adapt open material, base entries on peer-reviewed publications,
    and present them in a readable form. The site is informational and
    popular-science in nature.
  </p>
  <p style="margin-top: var(--space-3);">
    <a href="{{ '/en/o-proekte/' | url }}">More about the project →</a>
  </p>
</section>
